            "title": "Show HN: I trained a 125M model to autocomplete piano on-device",
            "description": "<p>I trained a 125M-parameter transformer to autocomplete piano performances in real time (~108 notes/sec on an iPhone 15).<p>The idea is basically GitHub Copilot or Tabnine, except instead of prompting it with code, you prompt it by playing a few notes on a MIDI piano. The model then continues what you played, entirely on-device.<p>The app is free if anyone wants to try it. Happy to answer questions about the model, training, Core ML, or the many things that didn't work.</p>\n<hr />\n<p>Comments URL: <a href=\"https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=49373456\">https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=49373456</a></p>\n<p>Points: 50</p>\n<p># Comments: 9</p>",
